1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,742
Which city sold the most?

2
00:00:01,962 --> 00:00:02,963
Let's find out!

3
00:00:03,183 --> 00:00:05,443
This is Data Analytics, Part

4
00:00:05,443 --> 00:00:06,815
10: SQL GROUP BY.

5
00:00:07,035 --> 00:00:08,519
Here is our sales table.

6
00:00:09,239 --> 00:00:10,555
GROUP BY puts rows

7
00:00:10,555 --> 00:00:11,870
with the same city

8
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:12,893
into one pile.

9
00:00:13,113 --> 00:00:14,194
Then SUM adds

10
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:15,274
up each pile.

11
00:00:15,494 --> 00:00:16,224
You get one

12
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:17,086
row per city.

13
00:00:17,806 --> 00:00:19,328
Select city and the sum

14
00:00:19,328 --> 00:00:21,115
of sales, from sales, group

15
00:00:21,115 --> 00:00:22,636
by city, biggest first.

16
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,793
Delhi has three fifty, Pune

17
00:00:24,793 --> 00:00:26,371
two ten, Mumbai sixty.

18
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:28,056
Put it on a chart

19
00:00:28,056 --> 00:00:29,474
and the answer jumps out.

20
00:00:29,694 --> 00:00:30,607
Delhi wins with

21
00:00:30,607 --> 00:00:31,825
three hundred fifty.

22
00:00:32,545 --> 00:00:34,008
To count orders per

23
00:00:34,008 --> 00:00:35,239
city, do you use

24
00:00:35,239 --> 00:00:36,240
SUM or COUNT?

25
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:37,839
Pick one in the comments!

